          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On January 1, 2014 at 12:15 am, several people were intrigued by the silent movements of a light in the sky. A photograph was taken. The observation of a red-orange light moving slowly on a festive night suggests a Thai lantern. Meteociel indicates a light south wind: weather not incompatible with a southwest to northeast movement indicated by the witness. The photo provided, greatly enlarged, and likely subject to camera shake blur, is consistent with this hypothesis. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\": probable observation of a Thai lantern.",
